---
onetaskgraph_template: 1
description: >-
  The spikes of one plan, as a plan graph: the brief of what they will measure, the user's
  approval of it, and the spikes the draft adds. The draft creates it as `<plan>-spikes`
  only when the plan needs a measurement; the planning run's `spikes` step launches it in
  the same flow, and its `finalize` step reworks the plan from their reports. Finalize is
  not a member here because the engine refuses any node depending on a `publish:
  "preserve"` node, and every spike is one.
variables:
  plan:
    description: The qualified id of the plan whose spikes these are, `authoring:<native id>`.
    type: text
    required: true
  native:
    description: The plan project's native id.
    type: text
    required: true
members:
  - id: "{{ native }}-spikes-brief"
    title: "Write the spike brief of {{ plan }}"
    template: {file: spike-brief.md.j2}
    answers:
      plan: "{{ plan }}"
      native: "{{ native }}"
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: spike-brief
      onepipeline.persona: ../personas/spike-brief.yaml
      onepipeline.agent_graph: graphs/spike-brief.yaml
  - id: "{{ native }}-spikes-approve"
    title: "Approve the spike brief of {{ plan }}"
    template: {file: step.md.j2}
    answers:
      description: "Waits for the user's approval of the spike brief before any spike runs."
    depends_on: ["{{ native }}-spikes-brief"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: approve-spikes
      onepipeline.kind: human
      onepipeline.human_item:
        kind: task
        priority: medium
        title: "Approve the spikes of {{ plan }}"
        body: >-
          Read the document {{ native }}-spike-brief of {{ plan }}. Once the user approves
          the spikes it describes, run `just approve-spikes <this run's id>`.
---
The spikes of `{{ plan }}`: the spike brief, its approval, and each spike.
